# DROP hosted-MCP connector shim for claude.ai (PRD-040 / AGENT-DEPLOY.md path 2)
#
# claude.ai's "Add custom connector" dialog offers only Name + URL (+ optional
# OAuth). When the Request-headers beta isn't on your account, this shim lets
# you add a NO-AUTH connector at a secret URL while the DROP API key is injected
# server-side by Caddy — so claude.ai sees a working unauthenticated MCP
# endpoint and never handles your key.
#
# ── Install ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. Copy this file to the Caddy hosts dir on the box (imported automatically,
#    survives every Caddyfile regeneration):
#        <DROP_ROOT>/data/appconf/caddy/hosts/mcp-connector.caddy
#    (on example.com: /var/drop/data/appconf/caddy/hosts/mcp-connector.caddy)
# 2. Replace the three placeholders below.
# 3. Ensure DNS resolves the subdomain to the box (a *.<domain> wildcard covers
#    it). Use a DEDICATED subdomain, never the apex — two site blocks for one
#    host make Caddy's config ambiguous.
# 4. Reload Caddy (the platform reloads on config change; or `caddy reload`).
# 5. In claude.ai → Add custom connector, set URL to
#        https://mcp.<YOUR_DOMAIN>/<SECRET_PATH_TOKEN>
#    Leave OAuth Client ID/Secret blank. No auth needed on the connector.
#
# ── SECURITY ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The secret URL IS the credential: anyone who has it can deploy to your box,
# and it appears in your own Caddy access logs. Use a long random token
# (e.g. `openssl rand -hex 24`), treat the whole URL like an API key, and
# rotate by editing SECRET_PATH_TOKEN here. Prefer path 1 (Request headers) or
# path 3 (OAuth, PRD-041) if either is available to you.
#
# Placeholders:
#   mcp.<YOUR_DOMAIN>   — a dedicated subdomain (e.g. mcp.example.com)
#   <SECRET_PATH_TOKEN> — long random string, e.g. openssl rand -hex 24
#   <USER_ROLE_API_KEY> — a DROP user-role key (never admin); mint in dashboard
#   127.0.0.1:3000      — the DROP API port (default 3000; change if customized)

mcp.<YOUR_DOMAIN> {
    @connector path /<SECRET_PATH_TOKEN>
    handle @connector {
        rewrite * /api/v1/mcp
        reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:3000 {
            header_up Authorization "Bearer <USER_ROLE_API_KEY>"
        }
    }
    # Anything other than the exact secret path gets nothing.
    respond 404
}
